1
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,583
Well, your father needs to get going.

2
00:00:27,583 --> 00:00:31,375
Be good kids and listen to your big sister.

3
00:00:31,375 --> 00:00:33,625
--Where are you going?
--Don't leave!

4
00:00:33,625 --> 00:00:36,042
--Bring me something!
--I wanna go, too!

5
00:00:36,042 --> 00:00:39,625
--No fair!
--Let me come with you!
--Pretty please!

6
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:43,417
Sorry. I'm afraid not this time.

7
00:00:43,417 --> 00:00:47,208
--Huh? How come?
--It's not fair!

8
00:00:47,208 --> 00:00:52,625
Behave, you guys! Don't be selfish!
You're making it hard for him!

9
00:00:52,625 --> 00:00:57,292
Fine... Make sure all the kids get along.

10
00:00:57,292 --> 00:01:00,208
Yup! Good luck with your work!

11
00:01:00,208 --> 00:01:03,958
Thanks. I think it's time I head out.

12
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:06,333
--Take care!
--Bring me something!

13
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:08,083
Darling...

14
00:01:10,917 --> 00:01:14,833
I'm sorry. Take care of the kids.

15
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,667
Let's go.

16
00:01:26,208 --> 00:01:30,833
I suppose if I'm attacked,
it'll be during the speech?

17
00:01:30,833 --> 00:01:35,375
I can't say for sure,
but that seems the most likely.

18
00:01:35,375 --> 00:01:40,333
Only then will most of our brass
be gathered in one spot.

19
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:46,792
However, it's protocol to make escape
plans at the last moment for security.

20
00:01:46,792 --> 00:01:49,917
Naturally, VIPs will use carriages.

21
00:01:49,917 --> 00:01:53,583
Let's sit them at the
"special seats" on the edge.

22
00:01:53,583 --> 00:01:57,208
Clump them together as much as possible.

23
00:01:58,167 --> 00:02:00,667
Are you sure about this?

24
00:02:00,667 --> 00:02:06,333
Compared to our predecessors,
the Tyburs haven't been playing around.

25
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:10,292
We've been building relations
with the world's elite,

26
00:02:10,292 --> 00:02:17,083
improving the reputation of Eldians,
and watching Paradis Island's movements.

27
00:02:17,083 --> 00:02:21,042
But we should've been watching
our own backyard.

28
00:02:21,042 --> 00:02:26,167
Before we knew it, we had enemies
crossing the sea and at our necks.

29
00:02:26,167 --> 00:02:30,500
At this point, they might get
sliced at any moment.

30
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:35,125
It's the conspirators working with
Paradis who I fear most.

31
00:02:35,125 --> 00:02:38,667
We still don't know who they are.

32
00:02:38,667 --> 00:02:43,458
As you know, our motherland
Marley has many enemies.

33
00:02:43,458 --> 00:02:45,958
Some, in our own military.

34
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:50,167
We'll smoke them out
by lighting a fire under their asses.

35
00:02:50,167 --> 00:02:56,250
We can plan for their attack
and use it to our advantage.

36
00:02:56,250 --> 00:03:01,333
Unless you have a better idea,
we proceed as planned.

37
00:03:01,333 --> 00:03:05,625
Even if they take the bait,
we lose way too much.

38
00:03:05,625 --> 00:03:08,500
We'll sacrifice incompetent officers.

39
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:14,417
If the enemy's goal is to damage
Marley's military, it works perfectly.

40
00:03:14,417 --> 00:03:20,250
When you rebuild the military, the party
will approve whomever you choose.

41
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:23,208
But so many will die.

42
00:03:23,208 --> 00:03:28,000
Most of them will be Eldians!
They're spawn of the devil!

43
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:35,583
Don't change on me now, Commander Magath.

44
00:03:35,583 --> 00:03:42,458
You've sent countless Eldians marching
into machine guns and land mines.

45
00:03:42,458 --> 00:03:46,250
Why does it matter whether
they wear uniforms or not?

46
00:03:46,250 --> 00:03:49,458
Just keep doing what you've always done.

47
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:54,625
Let me say one thing:

48
00:03:54,625 --> 00:04:00,958
This isn't war. We don't know the enemy,
their goal, or how they'll attack.

49
00:04:00,958 --> 00:04:05,083
Plus, the venue will be packed
with a huge crowd.

50
00:04:07,708 --> 00:04:13,167
Lord Tybur, I doubt I'll be able to protect you.

51
00:04:13,167 --> 00:04:19,708
If we proceed, you will die.
They won't pass you up as bait.

52
00:04:23,125 --> 00:04:27,125
Of course. I'm prepared for that.

53
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:31,750
Unless I stand on stage,
the world will not take notice.

54
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:37,167
The military, newspapers, and
ambassadors won't gather in one place.

55
00:04:37,167 --> 00:04:44,375
Above all, the Eldians of the internment
zone and I must be made tragic victims.

56
00:04:46,208 --> 00:04:49,500
Victims of an "unforeseen attack."

57
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:55,250
If I am the sole survivor,
the world will not become our ally.

58
00:05:01,875 --> 00:05:06,333
There's no doubt that Eldians
are spawn of the devil.

59
00:05:06,333 --> 00:05:11,208
And there's no doubt
that we are devils ourselves.

60
00:07:07,958 --> 00:07:12,958
"The War Hammer Titan"

61
00:07:30,458 --> 00:07:32,958
Get up, Gabi! Udo!

62
00:07:32,958 --> 00:07:35,000
Stand up! Hurry!

63
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:39,833
Zofia?

64
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
--Zofia!
--Udo, don't!

65
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,833
--Zofia!
--Udo, get back!

66
00:07:47,792 --> 00:07:49,875
Hurry! We gotta lift this!

67
00:07:49,875 --> 00:07:51,208
Udo!

68
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:17,833
Brother... You fulfilled the
Tyburs' duty admirably.

69
00:08:42,875 --> 00:08:46,125
Commander! The War Hammer is getting wrecked!

70
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:47,833
Commander! The Warriors are missing!

71
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:49,625
--General Calvi and the brass are dead!

72
00:08:49,625 --> 00:08:51,042
--We should check for survivors!
--General Calvi and the brass are dead!

73
00:08:51,042 --> 00:08:51,875
--We should check for survivors!
--It's dangerous here!

74
00:08:51,875 --> 00:08:52,792
--We need orders!
--It's dangerous here!

75
00:08:52,792 --> 00:08:54,292
Commander!

76
00:08:57,042 --> 00:08:58,958
Commander?

77
00:08:58,958 --> 00:09:04,958
It's a useless plink, but this signals
the beginning of Marley's counterattack.

78
00:09:04,958 --> 00:09:08,167
To think they'd make such a grand entrance.

79
00:09:08,167 --> 00:09:15,167
What's more, it looks to be the usurper
of the Founding Titan--the Attack Titan.

80
00:09:15,167 --> 00:09:19,292
Eren Jaeger has come in person!

81
00:09:19,292 --> 00:09:24,625
Saves us a trip to the island.
Get in position! Prepare for battle!

82
00:09:24,625 --> 00:09:26,333
Yes, sir!

83
00:09:41,833 --> 00:09:44,292
Hey, what's all the ruckus about?

84
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:47,292
What are you doing?! We have to get out--

85
00:09:55,167 --> 00:10:00,583
Remember it, people.
I'm the one who took the first shot.

86
00:10:04,792 --> 00:10:08,292
Shit! What the hell?! It's a battlefield now!

87
00:10:08,292 --> 00:10:10,417
Colt! How's Udo?!

88
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:16,417
Not good. He needs the hospital.

89
00:10:16,417 --> 00:10:19,458
Udo! You're kidding!

90
00:10:19,458 --> 00:10:25,083
Shit! Falco! Where are you?!

91
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:30,833
What's happening out there?!

92
00:10:30,833 --> 00:10:35,208
By these tremors, I'd guess Titans are fighting.

93
00:10:35,208 --> 00:10:37,375
Are you serious?!

94
00:10:37,375 --> 00:10:41,083
Us being trapped down here
is answer enough.

95
00:10:41,083 --> 00:10:43,042
We've gotta get out somehow.

96
00:10:43,042 --> 00:10:44,542
How?

97
00:10:44,542 --> 00:10:46,208
What the hell?

98
00:10:46,208 --> 00:10:47,208
You're late!

99
00:10:47,208 --> 00:10:49,000
--Pieck!
--You okay?!

100
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,708
Throw us a rope!

101
00:10:50,708 --> 00:10:51,708
Got it!

102
00:10:51,708 --> 00:10:54,583
The Panzer Unit? How'd they know?

103
00:10:54,583 --> 00:10:58,292
I told 'em to follow since Beardy was shady.

104
00:10:58,292 --> 00:11:00,000
Back then?

105
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:04,417
This soldier seems shady. Follow behind us.

106
00:11:04,417 --> 00:11:07,000
A Titan attacked during the speech!

107
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
For real?!

108
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,958
The War Hammer is fending it off!

109
00:11:10,958 --> 00:11:12,583
Where's the Cart's gear?

110
00:11:12,583 --> 00:11:15,292
At HQ! We'll have it done in 15!

111
00:11:15,292 --> 00:11:16,333
Make it 10!

112
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:17,250
Roger!

113
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:18,583
I'm going ahead.

114
00:11:18,583 --> 00:11:22,083
Wait, Porco. Before you rush in...

115
00:11:22,083 --> 00:11:23,750
What the--?!

116
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:27,375
You're kidding... There's no way!

117
00:12:11,208 --> 00:12:14,333
--Yeah, it hit!
--Anti-Titan artillery packs a punch!

118
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:16,208
--Reload!
--Commander Magath,
let's finish off Eren Jaeger!

119
00:12:16,208 --> 00:12:17,667
--Commander Magath,
let's finish off Eren Jaeger!

120
00:12:17,667 --> 00:12:20,542
Without the Founding Titan, they're doomed!

121
00:12:20,542 --> 00:12:21,958
--No.
--Huh?

122
00:12:21,958 --> 00:12:25,417
Killing the Founding Titan
only postpones the problem.

123
00:12:25,417 --> 00:12:31,250
We need to have the War Hammer eat it!
We're here to ensure that happens!

124
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:33,917
B-But, Commander...

125
00:12:33,917 --> 00:12:37,833
I don't think the War Hammer
is trying to eat it.

126
00:12:46,458 --> 00:12:48,667
The War Hammer's a monster!

127
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:50,375
It beat the Attack Titan!

128
00:12:50,375 --> 00:12:52,625
The War Hammer wins!

129
00:12:58,250 --> 00:13:02,417
So that's Eren Jaeger, huh?

130
00:13:09,917 --> 00:13:12,875
It's really gonna finish him off!

131
00:13:14,542 --> 00:13:18,333
Usurper, Eren Jaeger.

132
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:22,500
Do you have any last words?

133
00:13:30,875 --> 00:13:33,250
Now or never, Mikasa.

134
00:14:12,375 --> 00:14:15,792
You guys actually came.

135
00:14:15,792 --> 00:14:18,667
Eren, please...

136
00:14:18,667 --> 00:14:20,458
Come home.

137
00:14:21,917 --> 00:14:26,917
"The War Hammer Titan is encased in a shell
created by its extraordinary hardening abilty.
It can use that same hardening ability to
construct any weapon it envisions at will."

138
00:14:27,958 --> 00:14:33,458
With the chain of command broken,
our military will be put to the test!

139
00:14:33,458 --> 00:14:38,583
Call down all our troops doing
special training in the mountains!

140
00:14:38,583 --> 00:14:44,000
Bring the fleet, too! Converge on top
of 'em with 30,000 soldiers!

141
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,375
I want Liberio surrounded!

142
00:14:46,375 --> 00:14:51,208
Don't let the Founding Titan
or a single island devil escape!

143
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:58,750
Have fun while it lasts.
There's no future for you now.

144
00:14:58,750 --> 00:15:04,917
With this massacre, you just ensured
every major nation gets involved now.

145
00:15:04,917 --> 00:15:11,000
The world will see the Eldian Empire
as a threat, just like Willy planned.

146
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,417
Now, no one's gonna let you live.

147
00:15:15,375 --> 00:15:20,000
But even they must've
known that going into this.

148
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,917
Which means...

149
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,375
You damn devils!

150
00:15:32,375 --> 00:15:34,458
Shoot 'em down!

151
00:15:39,542 --> 00:15:42,000
Those morons!

152
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,917
Hey! You gonna burn the whole zone down?!

153
00:15:44,917 --> 00:15:50,208
What part of keeping civilian casualties
to a minimum don't you get, Floch?!

154
00:15:50,208 --> 00:15:54,083
The only thing here are enemies
and places they live!

155
00:15:54,083 --> 00:15:59,250
Did you forget how they massacred
humanity inside the walls?!

156
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:03,042
We were eaten alive, dammit!
They've got it coming!

157
00:16:03,042 --> 00:16:05,000
You're still saying that?

158
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:09,750
Look. Eren's telling us something--to fight!

159
00:16:09,750 --> 00:16:13,250
We shouldn't just wait
for our deaths in the walls.

160
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:17,167
What we need... is a devil like him!

161
00:16:17,167 --> 00:16:23,833
Eren... Do you have any idea what you've done?

162
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,375
You killed civilians.

163
00:16:30,375 --> 00:16:33,375
You killed children, too.

164
00:16:34,292 --> 00:16:38,042
You've done things that can't be undone.

165
00:16:44,208 --> 00:16:48,167
Mikasa, it's not over yet.

166
00:16:48,167 --> 00:16:51,708
Impossible! I blew away its nape!

167
00:16:51,708 --> 00:16:55,125
And I crushed it with all my strength.

168
00:16:55,125 --> 00:16:57,583
Yet, it's not dead.

169
00:17:02,917 --> 00:17:04,750
I see...

170
00:17:06,792 --> 00:17:12,958
The War Hammer Titan... It uses
hardening to make whatever it needs.

171
00:17:12,958 --> 00:17:17,958
That must be why it won't die,
no matter what we do.

172
00:17:17,958 --> 00:17:24,083
Mikasa, get its attention.
If this works, I can eat the War Hammer.

173
00:17:26,625 --> 00:17:30,792
Sorry, we're at full capacity!
And the kid's dead already!

174
00:17:30,792 --> 00:17:33,167
Come on! At least look at him!

175
00:17:33,167 --> 00:17:36,500
Aren't you a candidate? Take a look around you!

176
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,083
We need you, doc!

177
00:17:38,083 --> 00:17:40,000
Okay, I'm coming!

178
00:17:43,417 --> 00:17:47,375
Gabi, stay with your family.

179
00:17:47,375 --> 00:17:53,667
I'm not sure if anywhere's safe.
Get as far from the plaza as possible.

180
00:17:53,667 --> 00:17:55,542
I'm gonna look for Falco and--

181
00:17:55,542 --> 00:17:57,333
I'm going, too.

182
00:17:58,250 --> 00:18:04,292
Because I don't understand
why Udo and Zofia had to die.

183
00:18:04,292 --> 00:18:06,583
Wait, Gabi! Don't!

184
00:18:12,208 --> 00:18:15,667
Hey, stop! You're headed towards a war zone!

185
00:18:15,667 --> 00:18:16,625
Gabi!

186
00:18:16,625 --> 00:18:18,500
What are you doing here?!

187
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:22,833
Mr. Gate Guard! I'll fight, so let me through!

188
00:18:22,833 --> 00:18:27,042
Don't be an idiot, brat!
You head back home and...

189
00:18:27,917 --> 00:18:29,417
--What the--?!
--Enemy attack?!

190
00:18:29,417 --> 00:18:30,875
From where?!

191
00:18:33,708 --> 00:18:35,542
--They're above!
--Shit!

192
00:18:35,542 --> 00:18:37,583
Go on, Gabi! Run!

193
00:18:39,042 --> 00:18:40,667
Hey, are you--?

194
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,208
Mister...

195
00:18:58,708 --> 00:19:01,750
This side's blocked off. Let's go, Sasha.

196
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:05,458
Conny... Did you forget about the lights?

197
00:19:05,458 --> 00:19:07,417
Oh, right.

198
00:19:28,875 --> 00:19:31,542
Jean, we stalled the reinforcements.

199
00:19:31,542 --> 00:19:32,958
And the lights?

200
00:19:32,958 --> 00:19:34,917
They're all in place.

201
00:19:34,917 --> 00:19:36,583
Are things going well?

202
00:19:36,583 --> 00:19:38,667
For the time being.

203
00:19:44,458 --> 00:19:48,042
As long as we take that thing out in time.

204
00:19:48,042 --> 00:19:52,458
But who knows?
Anything can happen at this point.

205
00:19:56,750 --> 00:20:03,833
What's to come when this battle is over?
For us to know, we have to survive.

206
00:20:20,667 --> 00:20:23,792
I knew something felt off to me.

207
00:20:23,792 --> 00:20:28,250
It didn't seem right how
the War Hammer appeared.

208
00:20:29,333 --> 00:20:33,875
And that's because its body
formed from the feet up.

209
00:20:35,333 --> 00:20:41,042
Not from its nape, but from
underneath the stage.

210
00:20:44,292 --> 00:20:47,375
Which means its body is...

211
00:21:17,583 --> 00:21:21,667
Shoot! The War Hammer
is about to get eaten!

212
00:21:32,292 --> 00:21:37,167
I've been waiting for this moment!
I'm retaking the Founding Titan!

213
00:21:38,125 --> 00:21:39,625
Eren!

214
00:21:42,458 --> 00:21:45,333
What?! I can't bite?!

215
00:21:47,833 --> 00:21:52,208
Was that him?! Is that... Ackermann?!

216
00:21:57,125 --> 00:21:59,125
This ain't looking good!

217
00:22:09,708 --> 00:22:13,958
You're kidding! Can't you see I'm a Titan?!

218
